dtprintinfo: build for SVR4, and fix the spool path buffers.

- libUI/BaseUI.h, objects/BaseObj.h: the bool-based boolean on SVR4, as on
  Linux; the fallback enum names its values false and true, which are
  keywords in C++.
- libUI/BaseUI.C: <sys/time.h> for struct timeval on SVR4.
- util/Invoke.C: assign SIG_IGN through sa_handler's own type.
- objects/PrintObj/ParseJobs.C: the SVR4 LP parser (spool files under
  /var/spool/lp) on SVR4, which runs the System V print service, as Sun
  does. In that parser, three snprintf calls passed sizeof of a pointer as
  the size of a PATH_MAX buffer, cutting each path to 3 characters, and
  the spool directory was formatted with the directory pattern as an
  argument instead of as the format; both now as the request path is.

